<title>CHINA: Japan's Yamaha to make pianos in China.</title>
<headline>Japan's Yamaha to make pianos in China.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Yamaha Corp has set up a $25 million, wholly-owned subsidiary in China's eastern coastal province of Zhejiang to manufacture pianos, the Xinhua news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Xiaoshan Yamaha Musical Instrument Co Ltd would be operational by July and would produce 50,000 pianos and 45,000 parts for other musical instruments annually, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>It had registered capital of $15 million, with investment totalling $25 million, the agency said. It gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
</text>
